<!--
  Clearpath Husky A300 with a UR10e, assembled from the unchanged upstream macros.

  The platform part is what Clearpath's description generator (clearpath_generator_common) writes
  for the sample configuration clearpath_config/sample/a300/a300_default.yaml: the common
  materials, the a300 macro in its default skid-steer configuration (control diff_4wd, outdoor
  wheels front and rear), the two bumpers and the top plate.

  The arm follows clearpath_config/sample/manipulators/arms/universal_robots.yaml (model
  universal_robots, zero offset on its parent) with ur_type ur10e, one of the types the
  configuration accepts.  That sample mounts the arm of a Husky A200 on default_mount; on the A300
  default_mount lies under the top plate, so the arm is put on top_plate_default_mount, the mount
  the plate itself provides at its centre.  The macro clearpath_manipulators_description/urdf/arm/
  universal_robots.urdf.xacro forwards its arguments to the ur_robot macro of ur_description and
  adds ros2_control blocks, which carry no mechanism; here ur_robot is called directly with the
  same arguments, and the links are prefixed arm_ as in the other robot records of this package.

  Arguments set by tools/build_robot.py: use_platform_controllers:=false (no ros2_control block).
-->
